{
  "part-2-page-004": {
    "html": "<p>Question: how would you spend \\(B_{\\mathrm{eval}}\\) evaluations?</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathcal X=\\prod_{j=1}^{p}[\\ell_j,u_j],\\qquad f:\\mathcal X\\to\\mathbb R\\]</div><ul><li><b>Random sampling:</b> draw points independently from a fixed distribution, e.g. uniform sampling.</li><li><b>Design:</b> choose points to cover the domain; no observed values are used.</li><li><b>Adaptive search:</b> use observed values to decide where to sample next.</li></ul><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}\\overset{\\mathrm{iid}}\\sim\\operatorname{Unif}(\\mathcal X),\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t\\]</div><p>First choose the information you can afford: dimension, cost per evaluation, budget and noise.</p>",
    "title": "Black-box optimization: sampling and designs"
  },
  "part-2-page-062": {
    "html": "<p>How can successful samples change the next search?</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf z^{(t,r)}\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf0,\\mathbf I_p),\\qquad\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}=\\mathbf m_t+\\mathbf L_t\\mathbf z^{(t,r)}\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf C_t=\\mathbf L_t\\mathbf L_t^\\top,\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t,\\qquad k_{t+1}=k_t+q_t\\]</div><ul><li>The mean \\(\\mathbf m_t\\) controls <b>where</b> we search.</li><li>The covariance \\(\\mathbf C_t\\) controls <b>which directions and scales</b> we explore.</li><li>Evaluate, compare, adapt; repeat until the evaluation budget is spent.</li></ul><p>These are random search directions learned from function values; derivatives are not required.</p>",
    "title": "Adaptive directional sampling"
  },
  "part-2-page-068": {
    "html": "<p>Gaussian adaptation (GaA): learn a Gaussian search region from accepted candidates.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,1)}=\\mathbf m_t+r_t\\mathbf Q_t\\mathbf z_t,\\quad\\mathbf z_t\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf0,\\mathbf I_p),\\quad\\det\\mathbf Q_t=1\\]</div><p>\\(r_t\\) sets the scale; \\(\\mathbf Q_t\\) sets shape and orientation; \\(q_t=1\\).</p>",
    "title": "Gaussian adaptation"
  },
  "part-2-page-069": {
    "html": "<p>Gaussian adaptation (GaA): learn a Gaussian search region from accepted candidates.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,1)}=\\mathbf m_t+r_t\\mathbf Q_t\\mathbf z_t,\\quad\\mathbf z_t\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf0,\\mathbf I_p),\\quad\\det\\mathbf Q_t=1\\]</div><p>\\(r_t\\) sets the scale; \\(\\mathbf Q_t\\) sets shape and orientation; \\(q_t=1\\).</p><p><b>Acceptance region</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathcal A_t=\\{\\mathbf x\\in\\mathcal X:f(\\mathbf x)&lt;c_t\\}\\]</div><p>\\(c_t\\) is a moving loss threshold. Evaluate the candidate once.</p>",
    "title": "Gaussian adaptation"
  },
  "part-2-page-070": {
    "html": "<p>Gaussian adaptation (GaA): learn a Gaussian search region from accepted candidates.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,1)}=\\mathbf m_t+r_t\\mathbf Q_t\\mathbf z_t,\\quad\\mathbf z_t\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf0,\\mathbf I_p),\\quad\\det\\mathbf Q_t=1\\]</div><p>\\(r_t\\) sets the scale; \\(\\mathbf Q_t\\) sets shape and orientation; \\(q_t=1\\).</p><p><b>Acceptance region</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathcal A_t=\\{\\mathbf x\\in\\mathcal X:f(\\mathbf x)&lt;c_t\\}\\]</div><p>\\(c_t\\) is a moving loss threshold. Evaluate the candidate once.</p><ul><li><b>Accepted:</b> move the mean toward the candidate, adapt the shape, and expand.</li><li><b>Rejected:</b> retain mean and shape, and contract.</li></ul>",
    "title": "Gaussian adaptation"
  },
  "part-2-page-071": {
    "html": "<p><b>Accepted candidate: learn from its direction</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\left(1-\\frac1{\\tau_m}\\right)\\mathbf m_t+\\frac1{\\tau_m}\\mathbf x^{(t,1)},\\quad\\tau_m\\geq1\\]</div><p>\\(\\tau_m\\) controls mean-update memory. Update the shape toward successful displacements and increase \\(r_t\\).</p>",
    "title": "Gaussian adaptation: learn from success"
  },
  "part-2-page-072": {
    "html": "<p><b>Accepted candidate: learn from its direction</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\left(1-\\frac1{\\tau_m}\\right)\\mathbf m_t+\\frac1{\\tau_m}\\mathbf x^{(t,1)},\\quad\\tau_m\\geq1\\]</div><p>\\(\\tau_m\\) controls mean-update memory. Update the shape toward successful displacements and increase \\(r_t\\).</p><p><b>Rejected candidate: reduce the search scale</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\mathbf m_t,\\qquad\\mathbf Q_{t+1}=\\mathbf Q_t,\\qquad r_{t+1}&lt;r_t\\]</div>",
    "title": "Gaussian adaptation: learn from success"
  },
  "part-2-page-073": {
    "html": "<p><b>Accepted candidate: learn from its direction</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\left(1-\\frac1{\\tau_m}\\right)\\mathbf m_t+\\frac1{\\tau_m}\\mathbf x^{(t,1)},\\quad\\tau_m\\geq1\\]</div><p>\\(\\tau_m\\) controls mean-update memory. Update the shape toward successful displacements and increase \\(r_t\\).</p><p><b>Rejected candidate: reduce the search scale</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\mathbf m_t,\\qquad\\mathbf Q_{t+1}=\\mathbf Q_t,\\qquad r_{t+1}&lt;r_t\\]</div><p><b>Why does this follow the landscape?</b> Directions that repeatedly produce acceptable losses influence the Gaussian’s orientation and spread.</p><p>The threshold and scale control how selective the search is. Detailed updates and parameter choices remain in the reference slides.</p>",
    "title": "Gaussian adaptation: learn from success"
  },
  "part-2-page-087": {
    "html": "<p><b>Sample</b> \\(q_t\\) candidates from the current search distribution.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}\\overset{\\mathrm{iid}}\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf m_t,\\sigma_t^2\\mathbf C_t),\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t\\]</div>",
    "title": "CMA-ES: sample, rank, adapt"
  },
  "part-2-page-088": {
    "html": "<p><b>Sample</b> \\(q_t\\) candidates from the current search distribution.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}\\overset{\\mathrm{iid}}\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf m_t,\\sigma_t^2\\mathbf C_t),\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t\\]</div><p><b>Evaluate and rank</b> by increasing loss. \\(k_{t+1}=k_t+q_t\\).</p>",
    "title": "CMA-ES: sample, rank, adapt"
  },
  "part-2-page-089": {
    "html": "<p><b>Sample</b> \\(q_t\\) candidates from the current search distribution.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}\\overset{\\mathrm{iid}}\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf m_t,\\sigma_t^2\\mathbf C_t),\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t\\]</div><p><b>Evaluate and rank</b> by increasing loss. \\(k_{t+1}=k_t+q_t\\).</p><p><b>Move the mean</b> toward the best \\(m_{\\mathrm{sel}}\\) candidates:</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\sum_{r=1}^{m_{\\mathrm{sel}}}w_r\\mathbf x^{(t,r:q_t)},\\quad w_r&gt;0,\\quad\\sum_r w_r=1\\]</div>",
    "title": "CMA-ES: sample, rank, adapt"
  },
  "part-2-page-090": {
    "html": "<p><b>Sample</b> \\(q_t\\) candidates from the current search distribution.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}\\overset{\\mathrm{iid}}\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf m_t,\\sigma_t^2\\mathbf C_t),\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t\\]</div><p><b>Evaluate and rank</b> by increasing loss. \\(k_{t+1}=k_t+q_t\\).</p><p><b>Move the mean</b> toward the best \\(m_{\\mathrm{sel}}\\) candidates:</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\sum_{r=1}^{m_{\\mathrm{sel}}}w_r\\mathbf x^{(t,r:q_t)},\\quad w_r&gt;0,\\quad\\sum_r w_r=1\\]</div><p><b>Learn directions</b>: covariance adaptation uses successful displacements and their accumulated history.</p>",
    "title": "CMA-ES: sample, rank, adapt"
  },
  "part-2-page-091": {
    "html": "<p><b>Sample</b> \\(q_t\\) candidates from the current search distribution.</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x^{(t,r)}\\overset{\\mathrm{iid}}\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mathbf m_t,\\sigma_t^2\\mathbf C_t),\\quad r=1,\\ldots,q_t\\]</div><p><b>Evaluate and rank</b> by increasing loss. \\(k_{t+1}=k_t+q_t\\).</p><p><b>Move the mean</b> toward the best \\(m_{\\mathrm{sel}}\\) candidates:</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf m_{t+1}=\\sum_{r=1}^{m_{\\mathrm{sel}}}w_r\\mathbf x^{(t,r:q_t)},\\quad w_r&gt;0,\\quad\\sum_r w_r=1\\]</div><p><b>Learn directions</b>: covariance adaptation uses successful displacements and their accumulated history.</p><p><b>Adapt scale</b>: \\(\\sigma_t\\) controls the overall step size; \\(\\mathbf C_t\\) controls shape and orientation.</p><p>GaA: one candidate and an acceptance threshold. CMA-ES: a ranked population and weighted recombination. Neither needs gradients.</p>",
    "title": "CMA-ES: sample, rank, adapt"
  },
  "part-2-page-053": {
    "bo": true,
    "html": "<p>Deterministic observations \\(y_i=f(\\mathbf x_i)\\).</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathcal D_k=\\{(\\mathbf x_i,y_i)\\}_{i=1}^k\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[b_k=\\min_{1\\leq i\\leq k}y_i\\]</div><p>\\(b_k\\) = <b>best loss observed so far</b>.</p><p>GP surrogate prediction:</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[F(\\mathbf x)\\mid\\mathcal D_k\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mu_k(\\mathbf x),s_k^2(\\mathbf x))\\]</div><p><b>Expected improvement</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[a_k(\\mathbf x)=\\mathbb E[(b_k-F(\\mathbf x))_+\\mid\\mathcal D_k]\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x_{k+1}\\in\\arg\\max_{\\mathbf x\\in\\mathcal X}a_k(\\mathbf x)\\]</div><p>Minimize the loss; maximize the acquisition.</p><p>Fit → acquire → evaluate → update.</p>",
    "image": "../blackbox-revision/bo-1.svg"
  },
  "part-2-page-054": {
    "bo": true,
    "html": "<p>Deterministic observations \\(y_i=f(\\mathbf x_i)\\).</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathcal D_k=\\{(\\mathbf x_i,y_i)\\}_{i=1}^k\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[b_k=\\min_{1\\leq i\\leq k}y_i\\]</div><p>\\(b_k\\) = <b>best loss observed so far</b>.</p><p>GP surrogate prediction:</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[F(\\mathbf x)\\mid\\mathcal D_k\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mu_k(\\mathbf x),s_k^2(\\mathbf x))\\]</div><p><b>Expected improvement</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[a_k(\\mathbf x)=\\mathbb E[(b_k-F(\\mathbf x))_+\\mid\\mathcal D_k]\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x_{k+1}\\in\\arg\\max_{\\mathbf x\\in\\mathcal X}a_k(\\mathbf x)\\]</div><p>Minimize the loss; maximize the acquisition.</p><p>Fit → acquire → evaluate → update.</p>",
    "image": "../blackbox-revision/bo-2.svg"
  },
  "part-2-page-055": {
    "bo": true,
    "html": "<p>Deterministic observations \\(y_i=f(\\mathbf x_i)\\).</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathcal D_k=\\{(\\mathbf x_i,y_i)\\}_{i=1}^k\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[b_k=\\min_{1\\leq i\\leq k}y_i\\]</div><p>\\(b_k\\) = <b>best loss observed so far</b>.</p><p>GP surrogate prediction:</p><div class=\"equation\">\\[F(\\mathbf x)\\mid\\mathcal D_k\\sim\\mathcal N(\\mu_k(\\mathbf x),s_k^2(\\mathbf x))\\]</div><p><b>Expected improvement</b></p><div class=\"equation\">\\[a_k(\\mathbf x)=\\mathbb E[(b_k-F(\\mathbf x))_+\\mid\\mathcal D_k]\\]</div><div class=\"equation\">\\[\\mathbf x_{k+1}\\in\\arg\\max_{\\mathbf x\\in\\mathcal X}a_k(\\mathbf x)\\]</div><p>Minimize the loss; maximize the acquisition.</p><p>Fit → acquire → evaluate → update.</p>",
    "image": "../blackbox-revision/bo-3.svg"
  },
